Z||000003||fotofrank||11-09-2001||04:28 PM||||I've got the same problem but intermittantly. Could be the solinoid for the started, bad connection at the solinoit, battery posts carroded, loose connection at battrery, bad groung. I have tried most the the possible causes but because mine is intermittant I can not tell if I fixed anything or not. Once I got the car started it may start 8 to 10 times before failing and not the same day! Good luck<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||11
Z||000004||johnt671||11-09-2001||06:24 PM||||If you have juice to the starter and the car won't turn over you have a bad starter.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Return of Fiero||11-10-2001||10:32 PM||||maybe i should have stated tests i have done to help everyone troubleshoot. i have put a hot lead to the switched post on the solenoid, and the engine cranked over. i tried it a few times, and found no bad spots on the starter. i have also tried to test the neutral safety switch, but turning the ignition to start and holding it while i pulled the gear selector down from park to 1 (or L, i dont really know, as this is my first auto, and i havent driven it) other things i have tried have been electrical test, simple ones as testing for power, and testing the amount of power on the end of the wires on the starter.<P>tanks for the help<BR>Myke||||reg||1
